<article class="env-lemma" id="0CCB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CCB">Lemma <span data-tag="0CCB">33.36.6</span>.</a> Let $p > 0$ be a prime number. Let $S$ be a scheme in characteristic $p$. Let $X$ be a scheme over $S$. Then the relative frobenius $F_{X/S} : X \to X^{(p)}$ is a universal homeomorphism, is integral, and induces purely inseparable residue field extensions. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0CC8" data-tag="0CC8">33.36.3</a> the morphisms $F_ X : X \to X$ and the base change $h : X^{(p)} \to X$ of $F_ S$ are universal homeomorphisms. Since $h \circ F_{X/S} = F_ X$ we conclude that $F_{X/S}$ is a universal homeomorphism (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0H2M" data-tag="0H2M">29.46.8</a>). By Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/04DF" data-tag="04DF">29.46.5</a> and <a href="/tag/01S4" data-tag="01S4">29.10.2</a> we conclude that $F_{X/S}$ has the other properties as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>